will look at: intersexuality and supernumerary\u00a0genders; physical and cultural reproduction; sexuality; and sex-based and\u00a0gender-based violence and\u00a0power. We will use lectures, films, discussion sections and short field-based exercises.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "(GLC-AS, SBA-AS, SCD-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(EC-LASP)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2853, "crseId": 373312, "crseOfferNbr": 3, "subject": "LGBT", "catalogNbr": "3635", "titleShort": "Queer Classics", "titleLong": "Queer Classics", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 19254, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:25PM", "timeEnd": "02:40PM", "startDt": "08/21/2023", "endDt": "12/04/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "cjl299", "firstName": "Cat", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Lambert"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "Goldwin Smith Hall 122", "bldgDescr": "Goldwin Smith Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "GSH122", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/21/2023", "endDt": "12/16/2023", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "CLASS", "catalogNbr": "3635", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "FGSS", "catalogNbr": "3636", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "SHUM", "catalogNbr": "3635", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "08/21/2023", "sessionEndDt": "12/16/2023", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This course engages classical antiquity and its reception through the prism of queer studies. Cruising Homer, Sappho, Euripides, Plato, Ovid and more, we will explore how queer theoretical frameworks help us account for premodern queer and trans bodies, desires, experiences, and aesthetics. We will trace how people historically have engaged with the classical past in political and affective projects of writing queer history and literature, constructing identities and communities, and imagining queer futures. We will unpack how classical scholarship might reproduce contemporary forms of homophobia and transphobia in its treatments of gender, sexuality, and embodiment in the classical past, and in turn how modern uses of the classical might reinforce or dismantle exclusionary narratives around 'queerness' today as it intersects with race, gender, sexuality, and class. Finally, we will consider how the work we are doing in this class (where the 'Queer' in 'Queer Classics' may be taken as an adjective or an imperative) relates to the ways that contemporary writers, activists, artists, and performers have animated the classical past with queer possibilities. All readings will be in translation; no knowledge of Latin and Greek is required.", "catalogBreadth": "(HB)", "catalogDistr": "(ALC-AS, LA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalo